Z||000002||Devotshka||12-10-2001||08:16 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jegs.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.summit.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.summit.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.jcwhitney.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jcwhitney.com</A> <P>Among others.... you are going to have to go to your local hardware store to get the fittings to adapt it to the fuel rail, you'll have a tough time finding one with the correct fittings for a fiero from anywhere other than TFS.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88-DOHC||12-10-2001||08:21 PM||||Should be available from tons of places, as places like AutoMeter and VDO make fuel pressure gauges. For all I know the one your talking about is probably a VDO gauge. There are other gauge manufactures out there. So I am sure you should be able to find something.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||12-10-2001||08:32 PM||||Since you cant get R-12 anymore, I just use my old low pressure gauge to read the fuel pressure. The fitting on the R-12 hose is the same as the valve in the fuel rail.||||reg||1
